;; definition for method 64 of type vehicle
;; og:preserve-this vehicle shadow-ctrl rung (falcon post-spawn crash): partial
;; landing of retail's method 64, ops 13-26 only (vehicle_ir2.asm:2499 in the
;; jak3 twin corpus). Retail allocates this vehicle's shadow-control and
;; stores it at draw+144 BEFORE dispatching the base rigid-body-object-
;; method-64 body, whose own base method 68 call writes into this same
;; shadow-ctrl; the allocation must precede call-parent-method to preserve
;; that ordering for a future method-68 landing. Without this, wvehicle.gc's
;; shadow block (wvehicle.gc:472, `(-> this draw shadow-ctrl settings)`)
;; dereferences the process-drawable.gc:672 #f default unguarded, and #f plus
;; offset 28 gives the unaligned 0x147d3d that faults vector+float*!'s first
;; aligned load. (shadow-flags shdf03) is bit 3 = 8, matching retail's addiu
;; t2, r0, 8 (shadow-cpu-h.gc:9-21); the shadow-control new method
;; (shadow-cpu-h.gc:227-248, landed) initializes shadow-dir aligned, so this
;; alone clears the fault. Do not null-guard the wvehicle.gc dereference
;; instead: retail always allocates before that read, so a guard would
;; silently kill vehicle shadows and dead-end method 68's future stores. The
;; full retail body also dispatches vehicle-method-99/110/50/51 and
;; collide-shape-method-46, still zero slots; the verbatim landing is a
;; future priced rung once those callees land.
;;
;; og:preserve-this panel-placement rung (issue 571 root cause, piece 2):
;; the dotimes-12 section dispatch loop below is added after call-parent-
;; method, matching retail's own placement (a fresh scoped decode of the
;; vehicle object, this rung's own tooling, ops 240-258; the raw asm
;; sequence right after the ja-post/status-flag block ops 13-26's own
;; landing stops short of). Per section (gp+1020+64*i machine, the +4
;; basic-tag correction over `sections`'s own :offset-assert 1024 landing
;; on the same stride the vehicle-h.gc deftype already declares :inline):
;; op 245 reads the section's own machine offset 24 (draw, unshifted --
;; vehicle-section is a plain structure, not basic-derived) and op 246
;; skips the whole body when it is zero. Inside: op 247 stores the loop
;; index at machine offset 55 (car-part); ops 248-252 dispatch vehicle-
;; section-method-10 with the section as `this` and this vehicle (gp) as
;; arg0, matching the signature landed on a sibling branch (issue 571
;; piece 1, rebased into this one at train time -- this loop is what
;; actually calls it, since method 10 was reachable from nowhere else in
;; this worktree before this loop existed); ops 253-256 store the literal
;; 30 into the section's own draw-control at offset 128 (light-index),
;; the identical idiom method 64's own already-landed block (ops 219-221)
;; uses to set light-index on the vehicle's own draw. Sections are built
;; by (method 66 vehicle, unlanded) and (method 68 vehicle, landed issue
;; 571 R11) repoints each section's own info pointer before this loop
;; runs on every subsequent call to method 64, per the investigation's
;; own ordering proof.
(defmethod rigid-body-object-method-64 ((this vehicle) (arg0 object))
  (set! (-> this draw shadow-ctrl)
        (new 'process 'shadow-control -61440.0 -2048.0 69632.0 (-> this root trans) (shadow-flags shdf03) 245760.0)
        )
  (call-parent-method this arg0)
  (dotimes (i 12)
    (when (nonzero? (-> this sections i draw))
      (set! (-> this sections i car-part) i)
      (vehicle-section-method-10 (-> this sections i) this)
      (set! (-> this sections i draw light-index) 30)
      )
    )
  0
  (none)
  )
